published yesterday so we have the press  release on the D bps the DEF budgetary  plans published the Greek statements the  reappointment of the euro working group  chair and there are a number of  documents that were going to publish  soon then the letter of the president  sent a note to president Michel which is  the outcome of this meeting the ESM  related documents and the reports of the  high level working group chair on the  banking Union Commissioner thank you  first of all thank you very much Mario  for your kind words  it was in fact my first Eurogroup and  I'm grateful to Mario that you were  capable to end it before midnight it was  three minutes before midnight eight  minutes before midnight  yes we presented our reports on Greece  on Cyprus and on Spain about Greece I  have to say that I had on Tuesday a very  positive meeting with the finance  minister Christos stai chorus and that  the country according to our report is  well on the road to recovery  obviously as Mario said challenges  remain but government is strongly  committed to face these challenges and  also yesterday during the discussion  that we had in the Euro group the  minister was very clear about these  commitments and so the council moved  forward for this decision of the  disbursements of 767 millions following  the agreement that we had last year so  good news for Greece from this point of  view and  the Commission and ESM will continue in  their cooperation with the Greek  authorities I have to say that we had an  interesting and good discussion on the  draft budgetary plans not so much on the  single draft budgetary plan of the 19  countries in this case I present the  opinions adopted by the Commission but  on the general fiscal policies and I am  convinced that we need more than ever to  have coordinated and differentiated  fiscal policies we are not 19 separate  economies we are a monetary and economic  Union and I think we should work in the  next year's to build on this concept